<title>UK: BAe, Lockheed to bid for army deal.</title>
<headline>BAe, Lockheed to bid for army deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Aerospace Plc and U.S. aircraft maker Lockheed Martin Corp said on Thursday that they would bid for a new U.S. and British army scout car and reconnaisance vehicle.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Lockheed told Reuters the deal was worth a potential five billion dollars &quot;if the U.S. and British armies order what they say they need.&quot;</p>
</text>
